From: Google Mozc upstream <https://github.com/google/mozc/commit/29c082a64b577b661694148760a2ae19817beb57>
Subject: Remove leading "::" from custom widget class name in dictionary_tool.ui

Qt 6.12.0 uic rejects class names starting with "::" in UI files,
resulting in build errors (uic: Invalid class name). Drop the leading
"::" from the custom widget class.

Upstream issue: https://github.com/google/mozc/issues/1594
Upstream commit rebased onto the 3.34 sources (context differs from
master, change is identical).

--- a/src/gui/dictionary_tool/dictionary_tool.ui
+++ b/src/gui/dictionary_tool/dictionary_tool.ui
@@ -52,7 +52,7 @@
        <enum>Qt::Horizontal</enum>
       </property>
       <widget class="QListWidget" name="dic_list_"/>
-      <widget class="::mozc::gui::DictionaryContentTableWidget" name="dic_content_"/>
+      <widget class="mozc::gui::DictionaryContentTableWidget" name="dic_content_"/>
      </widget>
     </item>
    </layout>
@@ -78,7 +78,7 @@
    <container>1</container>
   </customwidget>
   <customwidget>
-   <class>::mozc::gui::DictionaryContentTableWidget</class>
+   <class>mozc::gui::DictionaryContentTableWidget</class>
    <extends>QTableWidget</extends>
    <header>gui/dictionary_tool/dictionary_content_table_widget.h</header>
   </customwidget>
